{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"MGASA-2026-0595","published":"2026-11-17T17:40:50Z","modified":"2026-11-17T17:58:38.674223558Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-121942","CVE-2026-88371","CVE-2026-95516"],"summary":"Updated zbar package fixes security vulnerabilities","details":"ZBar through 0.23.95 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in\n_zbar_sq_decode() in zbar/sqcode.c that allows attackers to read heap\nmemory outside the image buffer via crafted SQ code images. Attackers\ncan supply an image with a skewed SQ code finder pattern near the edge,\nproducing unchecked sample coordinates that crash the decoder and leak\nbytes into output.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"zbar","ecosystem":"Mageia:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/mageia/zbar?arch=source&distro=mageia-10"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.23.95-2.mga10"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"section":"core"},"database_specific":{"source":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0595.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0595.html"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugs.mageia.org/show_bug.cgi?id=36668"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://github.com/mchehab/zbar/issues/351"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/mchehab/zbar/releases#release-0.23.94"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/mchehab/zbar/releases#release-0.23.95"}],"credits":[{"name":"Mageia","contact":["https://wiki.mageia.org/en/Packages_Security_Team"],"type":"COORDINATOR"}]}